<title>SWITZERLAND: Fifth and final Swiss beet test shows higher yield.</title>
<headline>Fifth and final Swiss beet test shows higher yield.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's fifth and final sugar beet test showed higher beet weight and sugar content than last year, according to test results released by Zuckerfabrik + Raffinerie Aarberg AG.</p>
<p>Beet weight of 1,020 grams compared with 920 grams on average from 1991 to 1995, while sugar content at 18.2 percent was higher compared with an average of 16.1 percent over the previous five years.</p>
<p>The test was carried out on September 24. Details follow:</p>
<p>				 5th test 96  4th test 96  5th 95</p>
<p> BEET weight, grammes	 1,020	961	   775</p>
<p> Beets per hectare, tonnes   91.5	87.1	  71.4</p>
<p> Leaf-root weight ratio	 0.7	 0.7	   0.6</p>
<p> SUGAR content, percent	18.2	17.5	  16.7</p>
<p> Rain since April 1 (mm)    410.2     388.9	 509.1</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
